{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And the priest of Midian — El Reuel, the father of their father. If so, the name of their father is Yitro, and Ḥovav son of Reuel, mentioned before us in the portion of BeHa'alotekha — ויאמר משה לחובב בן רעואל — he is Ḥovav, he is Yitro. And if Reuel is Yitro, then he was a son of Yitro. And what is written in the Prophets: מבני חובב חותן משה — proves that Ḥovav is Yitro, for wherever 'the father-in-law of Moshe' is mentioned, it refers to Yitro."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Rashbam parses 'ולכהן מדין' as 'the priest of Midian,' resolving the identification of Reuel, Ḥovav, and Yitro through cross-references; the logical flow of his argument has been rendered as written, including the parenthetical-inference structure."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:13.245046381Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}